# SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000139  -  CAT II
# The web server must generate unique session identifiers with definable
# entropy.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000224-WSR-000139
group:           V-206403
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      tested
cci:             CCI-001188
control_rev5:    SC-23

contribution:    The entropy of a generated session identifier is not itself a configurable
                 quantity in Splunk Enterprise. What the application can do is select the
                 random source: in FIPS mode the instance is constrained to FIPS 140-2
                 algorithms and restrictions, which governs the generator the session
                 subsystem draws on.

governs:         splunk-launch.conf - Environment settings read before Splunk starts, including whether it
                 starts in FIPS mode.

check:           splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS equals 1 -> splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS in 1|true|t|yes (matched case-insensitively)
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The ratio of entropy to identifier length in a generated session ID - a
                 fixed property of Splunk Enterprise's session subsystem, with no setting
                 to define it; establish it by vendor attestation from Splunk
external:        The kernel entropy source available to the instance - operating system

citation:        splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-116 (SPLUNK_FIPS = [0|1], whether the instance
                 operates in FIPS mode and uses the algorithms and restrictions that apply
                 to FIPS Publication 140-2)
finding:         FIPS mode is not enabled, so the application does not constrain session
                 identifier generation to a FIPS 140-2 random source, which is its only
                 contribution to the entropy requirement; the entropy-to-length ratio
                 itself is not configurable and rests on vendor attestation.
